      "id": 1,
      "text": "Leon Valley grew from a 1940s farming community on Bandera Road between Helotes and San Antonio.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leon_Valley%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Huebner‑Onion Homestead, built by Austrian settler Joseph Huebner in 1858, once served as a stagecoach stop and now bears a Texas Historical Marker.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/leon-valley-tx",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Leon Valley Historical Society, founded in the 1970s, works to preserve the Huebner‑Onion Homestead and surrounding land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/leon-valley-tx",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Leon Valley is an independent municipality entirely surrounded by the city of San Antonio.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leon_Valley%2C_Texas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The city runs its own public library, offering community programs and a quiet place to read while driving past the historic streets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
